{
  "comment": "Same plugin-panel pattern as mopho.layout.json. Rows follow the JV signal path: patch common -> tone wave -> pitch -> TVF -> TVA -> LFOs -> control matrix -> outputs/FX. Tone groups share one select var {t} (1-4, 'all' writes all four tones); each tone group carries its own picker cell. Envelopes: the JV's pitch/filter/amp envelopes are 4-time/4-level (T1-T4, L1-L4; the amp envelope has L1-L3 and always ends at 0), not DADSR, so they are plain knobs here. The 'env' widget expects 5 DADSR keys; a T/L graph widget (keys = [T1..T4], levels = [L1..L4]) would be the natural addition. Wave: group (INT/PCM/EXP) is a seg, 'bank id' is the Wave Group ID (INT: 1 = INT-A, 2 = INT-B), 'wave' is a pick whose names come from schema.waves via the param's waveLookup (the editor needs a 'wave' display for that; until then it shows the number). The two LFOs and the three controllers each get their own group because the layout format has one select var per group (tone). EFX p1-p3 labels depend on EFX type (schema.efxTypes[efxType].params[n]). Tone pickers are linked (select.shared = 'tone'): choosing a tone in any group switches every tone group.",
